"αὐτάρ ( ἀvυτάρ IG 12.1012 ), Conj. = ἀτάρ ( Ep. and Cypr., Inscr.Cypr. 57 H.):—but, besides, moreover, prop. to introduce a contrast, Od. 13.286 , al.; also to mark a rapid succession of details, Il. 2.406 , al.; opp. μέν, Ἥφαιστος μέν . . αὐ. ἄρα Ζεύς . . ib. 102 sq., cf. Od. 19.512 sq.; αὐτάρ τοι but nevertheless, Il. 15.45 .—In an Epic reminiscence, Hermipp. 63.17 (hex.). αὐτάρ· αὐτομάτη, ἑκουσία, Hsch."